Version 2.3.1 brings a couple of GUI updates.

Features
- Switched from nanoVG to Cairo graphics backend. As it turns out,
  on Zynthian, nanoVG turns out to be very CPU consuming, as the 
  plugin UI screen is only accessible via VNC and hence completely in
  software (rather than supported by a GPU). nanoVG then needs to resort
  to Open GL emulation in software, which empirically seems to use a lot
  more CPU than Cairo. That in itself might be manageable, but when used in
  a snapshot together with certain other plugins, such as Osiris, the CPU
  load spikes during redraws due to parameter updates cause clicks and pops
  in the audio.
- Optimize redrawing when UI menu is open. The goal here is really to
  avoid all redrawing of parameters when the UI menu is open, as a workaround
  to eliminate CPU load due to redraws, should this be a problem in any setup.
- Added (small) waveform indicators around the Modulator 3 Shape
  parameter (which is continuous, not stepped like the other two
  modulators), and also infinity symbols at the top end of the
  ADSSR Sustain Time parameter value range, indicating that the envelope
  behaves like a standard ADSR when the Sustain Time is set to maximum.

As usual, a companion version 2.3.1z has been tagged on the Zynthian branch,
which supports the graphic envelope and filter display features in the Zynthian
UI.
